description:
Step 2 of the /plan notebook refactor epic. New server plan surface (Part B) + server half of the formula deletion (A3/A4). Independently testable via vitest.

## B1. server/src/plan-notebook.ts (new — canonical sidecar module)

Types (server mirror of client notebook/types.ts, cross-referencing header comments — same precedent as rename-all-server-types.ts):

```ts
interface PlanStep { id: string; componentType: "task"; type: "prompt" | "image" | "video";
                     name: string; properties: Record<string, unknown>; }
// well-known properties, read defensively:
//   prompt step: { text: string }
//   gen step:    { model: string; provider: string;
//                  values: Record<string, unknown>;   // full gen-form values incl. prompt + @slugs
//                  asset_ids: string[] }               // run history, oldest→newest; last = current output
interface PlanDefinition { properties: Record<string, unknown>; sequence: PlanStep[]; }
interface NotebookPlanSidecar { format: "notebook"; schema_version: 1; definition: PlanDefinition; }
```

Exports: emptyPlanDefinition(), isNotebookSidecar(v) (checks format === "notebook" — explicit legacy discriminant), zod planDefinitionSchema (top-level structure strict; step properties as z.record(z.unknown()); superRefine step-id uniqueness), renderPlanMarkdown(def), writePlanFiles(fs, projectSlug, def).

writePlanFiles: fs.getProject → mkdir(join(projectPath, "plan"), { recursive: true }) (the one sanctioned node:fs use, precedented in all 3 formula writers) → writePlanFileIfChanged(fs, slug, "index.md", renderPlanMarkdown(def)) → writePlanFileIfChanged(..., ".plan.json", JSON.stringify(sidecar, null, 2)). MOVE writePlanFileIfChanged here verbatim from plan-clip-show.ts:502 (keep its no-op-commit rationale comment — scoped git commits with no diff fail on dirty repos).

renderPlanMarkdown (deterministic, no timestamps, so unchanged plans no-op): "# Plan" header + step count; per step "## {n}. {name} — {type}"; prompt step → blockquoted text; gen step → **Model:**/**Refs:**/**Produces:** bullets (refs harvested defensively from values.image_slugs/first_frame_slug/video_slug; produces from asset_ids as @id) + blockquoted values.prompt. Empty sequence → "_No steps yet._".

## B2. Rewrite server/src/tools/read-plan.ts

Same name/schema (project_slug). Read via fs.readFile("plan", ".plan.json", slug) + own JSON.parse (not readMetadata, so corrupt JSON degrades gracefully; keep isMissingPlanError). Response (always JSON text):
- missing file → { exists: false, definition: emptyPlanDefinition() }
- parse failure or !isNotebookSidecar(parsed) (any legacy formula sidecar) → { exists: false, legacy: true, definition: emptyPlanDefinition() } — NO migration; file left untouched, first write_plan overwrites
- valid → { exists: true, definition }

## B3. New tool server/src/tools/write-plan.ts

write_plan — { project_slug: z.string(), definition: planDefinitionSchema }. Handler: validate → writePlanFiles → { ok: true, steps: n }; failures returned as { isError: true } content. NOT queued (small synchronous JSON+md write; same class as update_script). Do not add to activity-policy.ts exclusions (mutations should appear in activity; read_plan stays excluded). Register in tools/index.ts.

## B4. Adapt server/src/tools/rename-all.ts (updatePlanReferences, ~609–631)

Client form values store @-prefixed slugs (appendImageSlug normalizes to @img-x; server strips @), but rewriteDeep (rename-helpers.ts:481) only rewrites exact string matches and idMap holds bare ids. So: build an augmented map (old→new AND @old→@new) before rewriteDeep; after a changed rewrite, if the sidecar passes isNotebookSidecar, also regenerate index.md via renderPlanMarkdown so the mirror never goes stale. (Known, pre-existing limitation: ids embedded inside prompt text aren't rewritten.)

## B5. Server tests

- Rewrite read-plan.test.ts: valid notebook round-trip; missing → exists:false; legacy char_swap fixture → legacy: true; corrupt JSON → legacy-empty; missing project → isError.
- New write-plan.test.ts (createTestClient pattern): fresh-project write creates .plan.json + index.md and plan asset shows status "ready" in list_assets; read round-trip; identical rewrite succeeds (no-op path); invalid definition (dup step ids / bad type) → isError; index.md contains name/type/model/@id/prompt; overwrites a seeded legacy sidecar.
- Extend rename-all.test.ts: notebook sidecar @-slugs + bare asset_ids rewritten, index.md regenerated (convert any formula-shaped fixtures found there).

