The bottom control (Auto-arrange, Rows3 icon) renders as an unreadable solid green square — the user flagged it as 'not obvious what this does'. Cause: vendored @xyflow/react/dist/style.css:438-443 sets '.react-flow__controls-button svg { fill: currentColor }', which fills stroke-based lucide icons (Rows3, Undo2, Redo2 — all drawn with stroke, fill="none" attribute loses to the CSS rule) into blobs.

Fix — notebook.css, next to the existing '.vc-notebook-canvas .react-flow__controls-button svg' size rule (~:1332):

.vc-notebook-canvas .react-flow__controls-button svg.lucide {
  fill: none;
}

Scoped to svg.lucide because lucide-react stamps class="lucide lucide-<name>" on its svgs; xyflow's built-in zoom-in/zoom-out/fit-view glyphs are fill-based paths and must KEEP fill: currentColor, so do not blanket-override all control svgs. This also fixes the Prompt/Image/Video add icons landing in the stack via vc-uv6c.2. Keep the Rows3 icon and title="Auto-arrange" — rendered as strokes it reads as three rows (matches the track layout it produces).

Test — notebook-gen-ui.test.ts, in the css-reading test 'uses one emerald HUD shell...' (:38-52): add expect(css).toContain('.react-flow__controls-button svg.lucide').

Verify in dev: Undo/Redo/Auto-arrange (and the add buttons) show crisp stroked glyphs; the +/−/fit built-ins are unchanged; disabled Undo/Redo still dim (xyflow's :disabled rule uses fill-opacity — stroke icons dim via the button's color, confirm visually).

Move the three add-cell buttons from the floating horizontal toolbox into the left vertical React Flow <Controls> stack, then delete NotebookToolbox.tsx (taking the informational SNAP LOCKED chip with it — snapping is model-enforced via snapDefinitionToTracks, the chip toggles nothing).

PlanNotebook.tsx — in NotebookCanvas, extend the <Controls showInteractive={false}> cluster (:237-241). Handlers addFromToolbox, setDraggedStepType, clearDropPreview are already in scope (currently passed to <NotebookToolbox> at :242-246). Map over a local const (order prompt, image, video — mirrors toolboxStepSeeds) rendering:

<ControlButton className="vc-notebook-add-cell" title="Add prompt cell" draggable
  onClick={() => addFromToolbox('prompt')}
  onDragStart={(event) => {
    event.dataTransfer.setData('application/x-videocity-notebook-step', 'prompt')
    event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'copy'
    setDraggedStepType('prompt')
  }}
  onDragEnd={clearDropPreview}><MessageSquareText /></ControlButton>

…and likewise image (ImageIcon icon, "Add image cell") and video (Video icon, "Add video cell"). ControlButton spreads ...rest onto its <button> (@xyflow/react/dist/esm/index.js:4548) so draggable/drag handlers forward; className is merged, not lost. Resulting stack: zoom-in, zoom-out, fit (built-ins), Undo, Redo, Auto-arrange, Prompt, Image, Video. Drop handling is untouched (NotebookCanvas onDrop :114-154 reads the same dataTransfer key).

Delete: src/components/center-stage/notebook/NotebookToolbox.tsx, its import (PlanNotebook.tsx:40), and the <NotebookToolbox .../> element (:242-246). Add MessageSquareText, ImageIcon, Video to PlanNotebook's lucide-react import (:16).

notebook.css — prune .vc-notebook-toolbox* and .vc-notebook-snap-lock* everywhere; grep 'vc-notebook-toolbox|vc-notebook-snap-lock'. Whole blocks: :129-144 and :1265-1279 (toolbox container), :244-247 (toolbox svg), :1281-1298 + :1313-1317 (snap chip), :1300-1303 (toolbox-actions), and the @media (max-width:1100px) snap-lock rules ~:1697-1710. Grouped selectors :146-160, :162-166, :1305-1311 pair '.vc-notebook-toolbox button' with .vc-notebook-input-button / .vc-notebook-run — remove only the toolbox member, keep the others. Add a group divider before the add-cluster:

.vc-notebook-canvas .react-flow__controls-button:not(.vc-notebook-add-cell) + .vc-notebook-add-cell {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--vc-line-strong);
}

Tests — notebook-gen-ui.test.ts, 'renders stage rows...' test (:54-72): remove :57 (const toolbox = readFileSync(...NotebookToolbox.tsx...)), :67 (expect(toolbox).toContain('Snap locked')), :68 (expect(toolbox).not.toContain('Deploy')). Add on the notebook (PlanNotebook) source: toContain('application/x-videocity-notebook-step'), toContain('Add prompt cell'), not.toContain('NotebookToolbox'). model.test.ts is untouched (toolboxStepSeeds still used by addFromToolbox).

Verify in dev: click each add button appends the right cell on tracks; HTML5 drag from a ControlButton onto the canvas still shows the drop preview and places the cell (drag from inside the xyflow Controls panel is the one behavior to confirm by hand).

The React Flow controls cluster (zoom in/out, fit view, Undo, Redo, auto-arrange) renders at the vendored @xyflow/react default of 26x26px buttons with 12px icons — too small and unclear. In src/components/center-stage/notebook/notebook.css, extend the existing .vc-notebook-canvas .react-flow__controls-button rule (~line 1366):

.vc-notebook-canvas .react-flow__controls-button { width: 2.4rem; height: 2.4rem; border-bottom-color: var(--vc-line); }
.vc-notebook-canvas .react-flow__controls-button svg { max-width: 1.15rem; max-height: 1.15rem; }

(~38px buttons / ~18px icons.) All six buttons already carry title tooltips (zoom in, zoom out, fit view, Undo, Redo, and the auto-layout button whose title is handled in the node-cards task); no markup change needed.
